  "name": "daily-cap",
  "summary": "Allowed when spent today + this amount is at most the daily cap. Two pieces: an 8-bit adder, then a 9-bit comparison against the 8-bit cap.",
  "layout": "Lowest bit first everywhere. Order inputs: bits 0-7 = spent, bits 8-15 = amount, bits 16-23 = cap (24 inputs, 3 input bytes in that order). Piece 0 = Add(8, 8): a = spent, b = amount, 9 output bits (the sum, bit 8 is the carry). Piece 1 = GreaterOrEqual(8, 9): a = cap (piece inputs 0-7), b = the 9-bit sum (piece inputs 8-16), 1 output. Order output 0 = piece 1's answer = allowed (cap >= spent + amount). The sum keeps all 9 bits, so 255 + 255 = 510 is never read as 254.",
